# The build is not line-ending agnostic: the userscript embeds the stylesheets
# as JavaScript string literals, so a CRLF working tree bakes \r\n escapes into
# the bundle where a LF one bakes \n. The two artefacts are committed and then
# rebuilt on Linux in CI, which compares them, so the checkout has to be the
# same on both. LF everywhere, regardless of platform or of what a machine's
# core.autocrlf says.
* text=auto eol=lf
